{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `n_redcards`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the two indexed parameter prior statements `beta[1] ~ normal(0, 10)` and `beta[2] ~ normal(0, 1)` with a single vectorized built-in prior `beta ~ normal(beta_mu, beta_sigma)`. This preserves the same independent normal prior density while satisfying SafeStan's requirement that each top-level parameter be sampled exactly once using a plain identifier. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int N;
  array[N] int n_redcards;
  array[N] int n_games;
  vector[N] rating;
}
transformed data {
  vector[2] beta_mu;
  vector<lower=0>[2] beta_sigma;
  beta_mu[1] = 0;
  beta_mu[2] = 0;
  beta_sigma[1] = 10;
  beta_sigma[2] = 1;
}
parameters {
  vector[2] beta;
}
model {
  beta ~ normal(beta_mu, beta_sigma);

  n_redcards ~ binomial_logit(n_games, beta[1] + beta[2] * rating);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"n_games":[4,5,4],"n_redcards":[4,4,2],"rating":[2.254623436875526,2.258026770030493,3.856995666164553]}","protected_variables":["n_redcards"]}
